+# Slice 3.RV-ipc — fix round 1
+
+Board "Review a commit range" row 8. Original brief: `briefs/3.RV-ipc.md` (its Contract stands). Your round-1 patch is
+committed (`516810c`); the reviews are `.omp/run/notes/RVIpcBoundary.md` and `.omp/run/notes/RVIpcCorrect.md`. The real
+fixtures are committed (`a766541`: `frontend/fixtures/range/{review,empty}.json`). Owned is widened to the shared homes
+the reviews name.
+
+## Target
+
+Owned: `frontend/src/ipc/{fixtureRange,fixtureRange.test,fixture,fixture.test,fixtureCompare,fixtureCompare.test,
+tauriRange.test}.ts` (`tauriRange.test.ts` new).
+
+Read-only: everything else.
+
+## Blocks to fix (verbatim from the reviews; the first two are blocks, the rest promoted)
+
+1. **Test the committed cases** (`fixtureRange.ts:69`, SP5): in `fixtureRange.test.ts` add a test over the committed
+   cases with the default `files` (as `fixtureCompare.test.ts`'s `COMMITTED` does): `?range` lists 13 entries
+   including the renamed `docs/keys.md` and the deleted `src/api/mockBoards.ts`; each id's `loadRangeFile` gives, in
+   order: kindChanged, tooLarge, texts, texts, notUtf8, binary, texts, texts, texts, modeOnly, texts with mode changed,
+   texts, submodule; `?range=empty` lists none.
+2. **Test the Tauri source** (`tauriRange.ts:6`, all NoCoverage): `tauriRange.test.ts` in `tauriCompare.test.ts`'s
+   pattern (`vi.mock("./bindings", () => ({ commands }))`): `openRange` and `loadRangeFile` return camelCased domain
+   data; an `UnknownRangeFile` error comes back unchanged as `{ ok: false, failure }`; a texts reply with a negative
+   difference line rejects naming `differences[0]…`.
+3. **One shared Difference schema and one case parser** (`fixtureRange.ts:55`, `:93–104`): export `DIFFERENCE` from
+   `fixture.ts` next to `LINE_RANGE`/`SIDE_WORD_CHANGES`, plus one `parsedCases(schema, label, files, convert): Map<string,
+   T>` that owns the path → case-name rule; `fixtureCompare.ts` and `fixtureRange.ts` both use them.
+4. **Closed lists typed by the generated unions** (`fixtureRange.ts:29`, `:74`, TS17): export `memberOf` from
+   `fixture.ts`; `ENTRY_KINDS: Readonly<Record<Generated.RangeEntryKind, true>>` and `RANGE_SIDES:
+   Readonly<Record<Generated.RangeSides, true>>` passed to it, replacing the two `v.picklist`s.
+5. **Pin the no-parameter default** (`fixtureRange.ts:117`): add `""` to the `test.each(["?range", "?range="])` of
+   "%s without a case loads review".
+
+## Acceptance
+
+All of the above; every earlier test passes (the compare fixtures unchanged in behaviour); typecheck proves a missing
+member in `ENTRY_KINDS` fails. Your tests kill the mutants on your lines (Stryker, SP5).
+
+Commands: `pnpm -C frontend typecheck`, `pnpm -C frontend lint`, `pnpm -C frontend test`, `pnpm -C frontend fmt:check`,
+`pnpm -C frontend unused`.
+
+## Skills
+
+`skill://ts-conventions`, `skill://ipc-contract` (plus your autoloaded ones).
